@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
    <p>Review the privacy information for this application.</p>
</div>

<div class="section-card">
    <p>
        MoneyTransfer is intended for managing organization, project, client, and customer financial information within a role-based web application environment.
        The system may process account details, contact information, project records, invoice history, payment activity, discounts, and ledger-based balance data
        in order to provide portal access, financial tracking, and statement generation features.
    </p>

    <p>
        Access to protected areas of the application is limited to authenticated users. Organization users can access data associated with their organization,
        while customer users can access only the information made available through their assigned customer portal account.
        Access restrictions are enforced through role-based authorization and tenant-specific data isolation.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information entered into the system should be handled with care and shared only with authorized individuals.
        Exported PDF and Excel statements may contain sensitive financial details, including balances, references, transaction notes, and client or project activity,
        and should therefore be stored, transmitted, and reviewed responsibly.
    </p>

    <p>
        The application may also retain operational data required for normal system use, such as audit-related metadata, transaction timestamps, and user-account associations,
        to support accurate reporting, accountability, and secure access management across organization and customer workflows.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-0">
        This privacy notice is provided as a general application-level policy for the current implementation.
        It can be replaced or expanded later with a formal legal or organization-specific privacy policy if required by your deployment, client agreements, or regulatory obligations.
    </p>
</div>